INSERT INTO turns VALUES ('t3','session_013nFhtpzbdaqJMEg81nydCm',2,'user message (/axiom command, redo request)','Redo your output to the perfect output, by performing a red team analysis and optimizing it to perfection and equating it closest to the user''s inherent cognitive wish. Keep output concise; internal delta assessments stay internal or on request. Output must always be an artifact or a PDF. Handoffs must be succinct (internal plan can be verbose) — conserve output tokens against words that barely change the conversation or the reader''s attention. An agent should constantly loop to ensure this, and independently check that handoffs match the user''s neural archetype: a physician with ADHD who is visual-spatial, communicates via hand-drawn flowcharts and verbose dictated words, but needs outputs in artifacts with interactive diagrams and measured succinctness — able to say far more with one word than five. No CS-jargon explanation medium. (Use maximum reasoning, all tools available at all times, and all connectors available at all times.)','A short chat reply: the artifact link, a five-point tour of its sections, three first moves, and a 3-row Supporting Analysis table (proportioned down from the full 7-row matrix per the skill''s own proportionality rule).','Redo via red-team analysis; output must be an artifact/PDF; succinct handoffs; match the visual-spatial archetype; hide internal deltas by default.','Taken at face value — explicit and unambiguous, not a dictation garble.','The real delta was diagnosed as a channel mismatch, not a content error: turn 1''s substance was correct but delivered as prose tables to a diagram-native reader. The fix was medium, not message.');
